Wrote the single-row label for Gail Griffin's `data-centers` topic to `coder-3.json`. Summary of the call: HB 2756 (2026), which she prime-sponsored and voted Yea on, requires cost-allocation formulas so large power users bear their own infrastructure costs rather than shifting them to residential ratepayers — this evidences the "energy cost-sharing agreements" clause of rung 3, but the bill has no impact-assessment or community-benefit-requirement provisions, so I coded `v6_value: null` / `v6_blank_reason: "compound-partial"` rather than committing to a specific rung.
